  "description": "Launch abort system (LAS) design: the solid or hypergolic escape tower that pulls a crew capsule clear of a failing launch vehicle within milliseconds. Covers the abort motor (solid propellant, 2-3 MN thrust, 2-6 s burn), attitude control motors for trajectory shaping, the escape jettison motor, and the structural load path that transmits 6-15 g escape loads through the crew couches.",
